Original commit body from f685e584efaaac4eacd61f94d9d7795c68091a86:

Measured with HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 on aardvark-dns: 669 nodes and
637 edges carrying origin=['scip'] -- 53% and 41% of the artifact --
entered from a pass that appeared in NEITHER analysis_runs NOR
limits.skipped_passes, the only one of 118 registered analyzers for
which that was true. All 1306 records had provenance resolving to
nothing: 1308 cross_field validation violations.

Three links, each individually reasonable:

1. analyzer.py's success path returned AnalysisResult(symbols, edges)
   with no run=, so AnalysisResult.run defaulted to None.
2. collect_analyzer_result records a skip only when a run-less result
   produced NOTHING; one that produced output was drained and then
   dropped from the accounting entirely.
3. translate_scip_to_hg satisfied Edge.__post_init__'s WI-higap guard by
   constructing an AnalysisRun purely to harvest its execution_id, then
   discarding the object.

The guard is why the two halves failed differently. Edge hard-raises on
an empty origin_run_id and Symbol does not, so the GUARDED half carried
a well-formed UUID resolving to nothing while the unguarded half stayed
honestly empty. An invariant written to prevent silent provenance loss
converted an abstention into a confident wrong answer.

translate_scip_to_hg has always taken run_id, and its comment says
callers wanting real provenance should pass one -- but
try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer had no such parameter to forward, so the
documented escape hatch was reachable only from tests.

This threads a real AnalysisRun end to end, stamps symbols as well as
edges at the translator (so a library caller bypassing the
orchestrator's empty-only WI-mosil backstop is still self-consistent),
and makes the orchestrator synthesize the run a productive run-less
producer failed to supply rather than dropping the pass. Recording a
skip there would be a lie: the output proves the pass ran.

TranslateFn is promoted from a Callable alias to a Protocol, since
Callable cannot express the keyword-only run_id and widening to
Callable[..., ...] would drop checking on the injection seam every
graceful-degrade test uses.

Repro re-run after the fix: 1308 violations -> 2 (an unrelated
fingerprint degeneracy and a stable_id collision), 0 of 669 nodes and
0 of 637 edges dangling, rust_analyzer present in analysis_runs.

Closes WI-didag
Closes WI-zabus

